      "content": "For the Double Declining Balance (DDB) method, the formula is:\n\nYearly Depreciation = 2 x (Cost - Salvage Value) / Useful Life\n\nHere's an example for a $100,000 asset with no salvage value over 5 years:\n\nYear 1: 2 x ($100,000 / 5) = 2 x $20,000 = $40,000\nYear 2: 2 x (($100,000 / 4) = $25,000\n Year 3:  2 x (($100,000 / 3) = $33,333.33 \nYear 4:  2 x (($100,000 / 2) = $50,000\nYear 5:  2 x ($100,000 /1) = $100,000 \n\nFor simpler example let's say only the yearly amount which would be \nYear 1: $40,000  \nYear 2: $25,000 \nYear 3:$33,333.33  \nYear 4: $50,000 \n Year 5 =$50,000",
